**Testing Time-Sensitive Logic**:

```javascript
const sinon = require('sinon');

describe('Token Expiration', () => {
    let clock;

    beforeEach(() => {
        clock = sinon.useFakeTimers({
            now: new Date('2025-01-01T00:00:00Z'),
            toFake: ['Date', 'setTimeout', 'clearTimeout']
        });
    });

    afterEach(() => {
        clock.restore();
    });

    it('expires token after 24 hours', async () => {
        const token = await createToken();

        // Token should be valid now
        let response = await request(app)
            .get('/api/protected')
            .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${token}`);
        expect(response.status).toBe(200);

        // Advance time 25 hours
        clock.tick(25 * 60 * 60 * 1000);

        // Token should now be expired
        response = await request(app)
            .get('/api/protected')
            .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${token}`);
        expect(response.status).toBe(401);
    });
});
```

**Mocking Best Practices**:

✅ Mock external services, not your own code
✅ Verify mocks were called correctly
✅ Reset mocks between tests
✅ Use realistic mock responses
✅ Test both success and failure responses

```javascript
// Good: Mock external service
nock('https://api.stripe.com')
    .post('/v1/charges')
    .reply(200, { id: 'ch_123' });

// Bad: Mock your own database function
jest.spyOn(db, 'saveUser').mockReturnValue(true);
```

**Key Insight**: Mock external dependencies to make tests fast and reliable. Use real instances of your own components when possible. The goal is to test your code, not someone else's.

