**Key Takeaways from This Example**:

✅ Tests are independent (each test creates its own data)
✅ Database transactions roll back after each test
✅ Authentication is properly tested
✅ Both happy paths and error cases are covered
✅ Business logic (like stock updates) is verified
✅ Security (authorization) is tested
✅ Helpers reduce duplication
✅ Tests are organized by resource and scenario

Status codes are the first indicator of API behavior. Testing them ensures your API communicates correctly about the outcome of each request.

**Status Code Categories**:

| Category | Range | Meaning | Example |
|----------|-------|---------|---------|
| **Informational** | 1xx | Request received | 100 Continue |
| **Success** | 2xx | Request succeeded | 200 OK |
| **Redirection** | 3xx | Further action needed | 301 Moved |
| **Client Error** | 4xx | Client made mistake | 404 Not Found |
| **Server Error** | 5xx | Server made mistake | 500 Internal Error |

**Common Status Codes and When to Test Them**:

```javascript
// Success Codes
pm.test("POST returns 201 Created", () => {
    pm.response.to.have.status(201);
});

pm.test("GET returns 200 OK", () => {
    pm.response.to.have.status(200);
});

pm.test("DELETE returns 204 No Content", () => {
    pm.response.to.have.status(204);
});

// Client Error Codes
pm.test("Invalid request returns 400 Bad Request", () => {
    pm.response.to.have.status(400);
});

pm.test("Missing auth returns 401 Unauthorized", () => {
    pm.response.to.have.status(401);
});

pm.test("Forbidden resource returns 403 Forbidden", () => {
    pm.response.to.have.status(403);
});

pm.test("Non-existent resource returns 404 Not Found", () => {
    pm.response.to.have.status(404);
});

// Server Error Codes
pm.test("Server error returns 500 Internal Server Error", () => {
    pm.response.to.have.status(500);
});
```

**Testing Status Codes by HTTP Method**:

| Method | Success | Created | No Content | Bad Request | Not Found |
|--------|---------|---------|------------|-------------|-----------|
| **GET** (collection) | 200 | - | - | 400 | - |
| **GET** (single) | 200 | - | - | 400 | 404 |
| **POST** | - | 201 | - | 400 | - |
| **PUT** | 200 | 201 | - | 400 | 404 |
| **PATCH** | 200 | - | - | 400 | 404 |
| **DELETE** | - | - | 204 | 400 | 404 |

