**Functional Testing Summary Checklist**:

✅ **Status Codes**
- [ ] Success codes (200, 201, 204)
- [ ] Client errors (400, 401, 403, 404, 409, 422)
- [ ] Server errors (500, 503)
- [ ] Rate limiting (429)

✅ **Request Validation**
- [ ] Required fields
- [ ] Data types
- [ ] Format validation
- [ ] Length constraints
- [ ] Range constraints
- [ ] Enumerations
- [ ] Edge cases

✅ **Response Structure**
- [ ] Field presence
- [ ] Data types
- [ ] Nested objects
- [ ] Arrays/collections
- [ ] Null handling
- [ ] Consistency

✅ **Headers**
- [ ] Content-Type
- [ ] Authentication
- [ ] CORS
- [ ] Rate limiting
- [ ] Cache control
- [ ] Location (for created resources)

✅ **Business Logic**
- [ ] Calculations
- [ ] State transitions
- [ ] Permissions
- [ ] Workflows
- [ ] Constraints
- [ ] Side effects

✅ **Schema Validation**
- [ ] JSON Schema conformance
- [ ] XML Schema (if applicable)
- [ ] Versioned schemas

✅ **Performance**
- [ ] Response time thresholds
- [ ] Consistency under load

**Key Insight**: Functional testing is the foundation of API quality. A comprehensive functional test suite gives you confidence that your API works as expected, handles errors gracefully, and delivers real business value.

One of the most common negative tests involves sending data of the wrong type. APIs must validate that each field receives the expected data type.

**Common Data Type Mismatches**:

| Expected Type | Test With | Example |
|---------------|-----------|---------|
| **string** | number | `"age": 25` as string vs number |
| **number** | string | `"price": "twenty"` |
| **boolean** | string | `"active": "yes"` |
| **array** | object | `"items": {"id": 1}` |
| **object** | array | `"user": [1, 2, 3]` |
| **integer** | float | `"quantity": 2.5` |
| **date** | string | `"createdAt": "not-a-date"` |

