**Key Insight**: Type validation is your first line of defense against bad data. Test every field with every wrong type you can think of.

APIs must handle cases where required fields are missing, optional fields are omitted, or fields are explicitly set to null.

**Missing vs Null Scenarios**:

| Scenario | What It Means | Expected Behavior |
|----------|---------------|-------------------|
| **Missing required** | Field not in request | 400 Bad Request |
| **Missing optional** | Field not in request | Use default or omit from response |
| **Null required** | Field present but null | 400 Bad Request |
| **Null optional** | Field present but null | Depends on API design |
| **Empty string** | String with length 0 | Usually invalid |
| **Empty array** | Array with 0 items | May be valid |

