**Key Insight**: Async message testing requires a different mindset. Instead of immediate assertions, you wait for expected outcomes. Use test doubles or real message brokers with careful isolation.

Third-party APIs introduce uncertainty. They may be slow, unavailable, or change unexpectedly. Testing these integrations requires a mix of mocking and selective real calls.

**Third-Party API Testing Strategies**:

| Strategy | Description | When to Use |
|----------|-------------|-------------|
| **Mocking** | Simulate API responses | Unit/integration tests |
| **Sandbox** | Use provider's test environment | Staging, acceptance tests |
| **Contract Testing** | Verify API contract compliance | CI/CD pipeline |
| **Canary Testing** | Small % of real traffic | Production monitoring |
| **Chaos Testing** | Simulate failures | Resilience testing |

