Test data management is critical for regression testing. Data must be consistent, repeatable, and evolve with your application.

**Test Data Challenges in Regression**:

| Challenge | Description | Solution |
|-----------|-------------|----------|
| **Data Drift** | Test data becomes outdated | Regular refresh, versioning |
| **Data Coupling** | Tests share data | Isolated data per test |
| **Data Volume** | Too much data slows tests | Subset of production |
| **Sensitive Data** | PII in test data | Anonymization |
| **State Management** | Tests depend on data state | Reset between runs |

**Data Versioning Strategy**:

```javascript
// regression/data-versioning.js
class DataVersionManager {
    constructor() {
        this.versions = new Map();
        this.migrations = new Map();
    }

    async registerVersion(version, data) {
        this.versions.set(version, {
            data,
            createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),
            schema: this.extractSchema(data)
        });

        await this.saveVersion(version);
    }

    async migrateData(fromVersion, toVersion, data) {
        const migration = this.migrations.get(`${fromVersion}->${toVersion}`);
        if (!migration) {
            throw new Error(`No migration path from ${fromVersion} to ${toVersion}`);
        }

        return migration(data);
    }

    registerMigration(fromVersion, toVersion, migrationFn) {
        this.migrations.set(`${fromVersion}->${toVersion}`, migrationFn);
    }

    async getData(version = 'latest') {
        if (version === 'latest') {
            const latest = Array.from(this.versions.keys()).sort().pop();
            return this.versions.get(latest).data;
        }

        return this.versions.get(version)?.data;
    }

    extractSchema(data) {
        if (Array.isArray(data) && data.length > 0) {
            return this.extractSchema(data[0]);
        }

        const schema = {};
        for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(data)) {
            schema[key] = typeof value;
            if (value && typeof value === 'object') {
                schema[key] = this.extractSchema(value);
            }
        }
        return schema;
    }
}

// Usage
const dataManager = new DataVersionManager();

// Register migration for data format changes
dataManager.registerMigration('1.0', '1.1', (data) => {
    // Convert old format to new
    return data.map(user => ({
        ...user,
        fullName: `${user.firstName} ${user.lastName}`,
        firstName: undefined,
        lastName: undefined
    }));
});
