**Session Best Practices**:

| Practice | Why It Matters | How to Implement |
|----------|----------------|------------------|
| **Timeboxing** | Prevents burnout, forces focus | Set timer, stop when time's up |
| **Note-taking** | Captures context, aids debrief | Use template, log as you go |
| **Single-tasking** | Deeper exploration, fewer distractions | One charter per session |
| **Regular debriefs** | Knowledge sharing, improvement | Schedule 15min after each session |
| **Metric tracking** | Measure progress, identify trends | Track findings, time, coverage |
| **Tool support** | Faster testing, better notes | Use session management tools |

**Common Session Pitfalls**:

❌ **No timebox** - Sessions drag on, lose focus
❌ **No notes** - Findings forgotten, can't reproduce
❌ **Too many charters** - Shallow coverage, context switching
❌ **Skipping debrief** - Knowledge lost, no follow-up
❌ **No metrics** - Can't improve what you don't measure

**Key Insight**: Sessions provide structure without rigidity. They make exploratory testing repeatable, trackable, and valuable for the whole team. A well-run session produces not just bugs, but knowledge, questions, and a clear path forward.

