**Key Insight**: Intuitiveness is about meeting developers where they are. Align with common patterns and conventions rather than inventing your own.

Beyond individual endpoints, test complete workflows that developers will actually implement. This reveals friction points that single-endpoint tests miss.

**Common Developer Workflows**:

| Workflow | Steps | Friction Points |
|----------|-------|-----------------|
| **Authentication** | Get key → Make first call | Key generation, first success |
| **CRUD Cycle** | Create → Read → Update → Delete | Data consistency, error handling |
| **Pagination** | Get first page → Process → Get next | Cursors, limits, performance |
| **Error Recovery** | Make request → Handle error → Retry | Error clarity, retry logic |
| **Bulk Operations** | Process many items → Handle partial failures | Batch limits, error aggregation |

