**Soak Testing Best Practices**:

| Practice | Why | How |
|----------|-----|-----|
| **Monitor Everything** | Catch early warnings | Real-time dashboards, alerts |
| **Track Trends** | Degradation is gradual | Compare hour-over-hour |
| **Check Connections** | DB connection leaks common | Monitor connection pools |
| **Watch Memory** | GC logs, heap dumps | Use APM tools |
| **Test Garbage Collection** | GC pauses affect latency | Monitor GC metrics |
| **Plan for Long Runs** | 24+ hours, weekends | Automated monitoring |

**Key Insight**: Soak testing reveals issues that only appear over time. A 24-hour test can prevent outages that would otherwise happen after weeks in production.

Scalability testing determines how well your API handles increased load by adding resources—either more power (vertical scaling) or more instances (horizontal scaling).

**Scalability Patterns**:

```
LINEAR SCALING (Ideal)
─────────────────────
Throughput
    ▲
    │        ┌───────┐
    │    ┌───┘       │
    │ ┌──┘           │
    │ ┘              │
    └──────────────────► Resources

SUB-LINEAR SCALING (Typical)
─────────────────────
Throughput
    ▲
    │        ┌────┐
    │    ┌───┘    │
    │ ┌──┘        │
    │ ┘           │
    └──────────────────► Resources

PLATEAU (Bottleneck)
─────────────────────
Throughput
    ▲
    │        ┌────┐
    │    ┌───┘    │
    │ ┌──┘        │
    │ ┘           │
    └──────────────────► Resources
```

**Scalability Testing Goals**:

✅ Determine if API scales linearly
✅ Find scaling bottlenecks
✅ Test auto-scaling configuration
✅ Optimize resource allocation
