**Key Insight:** Chaos engineering isn't about breaking things randomly—it's about controlled experiments to build confidence in system resilience.

Resilience testing verifies that your API handles failures gracefully. This includes testing timeout configurations, retry logic, circuit breakers, and fallback mechanisms.

**Resilience Patterns:**

| Pattern | Description | Test Strategy |
|---------|-------------|---------------|
| **Timeouts** | Limit wait time for responses | Inject latency, verify timeout |
| **Retries** | Automatic retry on failure | Inject transient failures |
| **Circuit Breaker** | Stop calling failing services | Inject repeated failures |
| **Bulkhead** | Isolate failures to one component | Exhaust one resource |
| **Fallback** | Return degraded response on failure | Force failure, verify fallback |

