Business logic flaws are vulnerabilities in the way the application implements business rules. They're unique to each application and can't be found by automated scanners.

**Common Business Logic Flaws:**

| Flaw | Description | Example |
|------|-------------|---------|
| **Workflow Bypass** | Skipping required steps | Checkout without payment |
| **Quantity Abuse** | Exceeding limits | Buying more than available |
| **Price Manipulation** | Changing prices | Setting your own price |
| **Coupon Abuse** | Reusing discounts | Applying coupon multiple times |
| **Race Conditions** | Timing-based attacks | Double-spending |
| **Function Order** | Calling functions out of order | Refund before purchase |

