**Mock Server Best Practices:**

| Practice | Why | How |
|----------|-----|-----|
| **Realistic examples** | Useful development | Use real-looking data |
| **Cover edge cases** | Test all scenarios | Include error examples |
| **Document examples** | Clear expectations | Add descriptions |
| **Version your mocks** | Track changes | Name examples with versions |
| **Use dynamic data** | Varied responses | {{$randomInt}} etc. |
| **Simulate latency** | Realistic behavior | Configure delays |

**Sample Mock Collection:**

```json
{
  "info": {
   "name": "User API Mock",
    "description": "Mock server for User API development"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "List Users",
      "request": { "method": "GET", "url": "/users" },
      "response": [
        {
          "name": "Success - Multiple Users",
          "code": 200,
          "body": {
            "users": [
              { "id": 1, "name": "John", "email": "john@test.com" },
              { "id": 2, "name": "Jane", "email": "jane@test.com" }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Success - Empty List",
          "code": 200,
          "body": { "users": [] }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Create User",
      "request": { "method": "POST", "url": "/users" },
      "response": [
        {
          "name": "Success - Created",
          "code": 201,
          "body": {
            "id": {{$randomInt}},
            "name": "{{name}}",
            "email": "{{email}}",
            "createdAt": "{{$isoTimestamp}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Error - Validation",
          "code": 400,
          "body": {
            "error": "Validation failed",
            "fields": ["email"]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

**Key Insight:** Mock servers enable parallel development. Frontend teams can start immediately without waiting for backend APIs. They're also invaluable for testing edge cases and error scenarios that might be hard to trigger in real APIs.

Beyond the basics, Postman offers powerful features for complex scenarios, performance testing, and API lifecycle management.

**GraphQL Support:**

Postman has excellent GraphQL support:

```graphql
# GraphQL query
query GetUser($id: ID!) {
  user(id: $id) {
    id
    name
    email
    posts {
      title
      comments {
        text
      }
    }
  }
}

# Variables
{
  "id":"123"
}
```

**GraphQL Testing:**
```javascript
// Test GraphQL response
pm.test("GraphQL returns expected user data", () => {
  const response = pm.response.json();

  // Check for errors
  if (response.errors) {
    console.error("GraphQL errors:", response.errors);
    pm.expect.fail("GraphQL returned errors");
  }

  // Validate data
  pm.expect(response.data.user).to.have.property("name");
});
```

**WebSocket Testing:**

Postman supports WebSocket connections:

```javascript
// WebSocket connection
// URL: ws://echo.websocket.org

// Send message
ws.send("Hello WebSocket");

// Handle response
ws.on("message", (data) => {
  console.log("Received:", data);
  pm.test("Echo server returns same message", () => {
    pm.expect(data).to.equal("Hello WebSocket");
  });
});
```

**Performance Testing:**

Run performance tests with Newman:

```bash
# Load test with 50 virtual users
newman run collection.json \
  -n 50 \
  --delay-request 100 \
  --timeout 10000 \
  -r cli,json \
  --reporter-json-export performance-results.json
```

**API Governance:**

Postman's API governance features help maintain standards:

```javascript
// Governance rules (example)
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "name": "All endpoints must have descriptions",
      "check": "collection.items.every(item => item.description)",
      "severity": "warning"
    },
    {
      "name": "Authentication required for all endpoints",
      "check": "collection.auth.type === 'bearer'",
      "severity": "error"
    }
  ]
}
```

**API Security Testing:**

```javascript
// Security-focused tests
pm.test("No sensitive data in response", () => {
  const response = pm.response.json();

  // Check for password exposure
  pm.expect(response).to.not.have.property("password");
  pm.expect(response).to.not.have.property("creditCard");

  // Check for security headers
  pm.response.to.have.header("X-Content-Type-Options");
  pm.response.to.have.header("X-Frame-Options");
});

