JSONPath and XMLPath are query languages for extracting data from responses. REST Assured integrates them seamlessly.

**JSONPath Basics:**

```java
public class JsonPathExamples {

    @Test
    public void basicJsonPath() {
        String json = "{" +
            "\"store\": {" +
            "  \"book\": [" +
            "    { \"title\": \"Book 1\", \"price\": 8.95 }," +
            "    { \"title\": \"Book 2\", \"price\": 12.99 }" +
            "  ]," +
            "  \"bicycle\": { \"color\": \"red\", \"price\": 19.95 }" +
            "}" +
          "}";

        JsonPath jsonPath = new JsonPath(json);

        // Simple paths
        String color = jsonPath.getString("store.bicycle.color");
        double price = jsonPath.getDouble("store.bicycle.price");

        // Array access
        String firstTitle = jsonPath.getString("store.book[0].title");

        // Length
        int bookCount = jsonPath.getList("store.book").size();

        // Find all titles
        List<String> titles = jsonPath.getList("store.book.title");

        // Find books with price < 10
        List<Map<String, Object>> cheapBooks = jsonPath.getList(
            "store.book.findAll { book -> book.price < 10 }");
    }

    @Test
    public void jsonPathInResponses() {
        Response response = given()
            .get("/store/inventory")
        .then()
            .extract()
            .response();

        // Extract using JSONPath
        JsonPath jsonPath = response.jsonPath();

        // Get values
        List<String> bookTitles = jsonPath.getList("books.title");
        double totalValue = jsonPath.getDouble("inventory.total");

        // Check existence
        boolean hasElectronics = jsonPath.get("categories").toString()
            .contains("electronics");

        // Get filtered results
        List<Map<String, Object>> discountedItems = jsonPath.getList(
            "items.findAll { it.discount > 0 }");
    }
}
```

**JSONPath Syntax Reference:**

| Expression | Description | Example |
|------------|-------------|---------|
| `$` | Root object | `$.store` |
| `.` or `[]` | Child operator | `$.store.book` |
| `..` | Recursive descent | `$..price` |
| `*` | Wildcard | `$.store.*` |
| `[start:end]` | Array slice | `$..book[0:2]` |
| `[?(expression)]` | Filter expression | `$..book[?(@.price<10)]` |
| `@` | Current node | `?(@.price<10)` |

