**Parallel Test Execution** [citation:3][citation:6]

One of Karate's standout features is its built-in parallel execution capability, which requires no special configuration or external tools:

```java
package runners;

import com.intuit.karate.Results;
import com.intuit.karate.Runner;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

class ParallelRunner {

    @Test
    void testParallel() {
        Results results = Runner.path("classpath:features")
            .tags("~@ignore")
            .outputCucumberJson(true)
            .outputJunitXml(true)
            .parallel(5);  // 5 threads

        // Assert that all tests passed
        assertEquals(0, results.getFailCount(), 
            "There were " + results.getFailCount() + " failures");

        // Generate reports
        // Results contain stats: getScenarioCount(), getPassCount(), etc.
    }
}
```

**Parallel Runner with Custom Options**

