**Priority-Based Stubbing**

When multiple stubs match, priority determines which one is used:

```java
// High priority - specific case
stubFor(get(urlEqualTo("/users/1"))
    .atPriority(1)  // Lower number = higher priority
    .willReturn(okJson("{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"John\"}")));

// Medium priority - all users except special cases
stubFor(get(urlPathMatching("/users/\\d+"))
    .atPriority(2)
    .willReturn(okJson("{\"name\":\"Regular User\"}")));

// Low priority - fallback for any user request
stubFor(get(urlPathStartingWith("/users"))
    .atPriority(3)
    .willReturn(okJson("{\"name\":\"Default\"}")));
```

