                .withBody("{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"John\"}"))
            .willSetStateTo("Cached"));

        stubFor(get("/users/1")
            .inScenario("User Cache")
            .whenScenarioStateIs("Cached")
            .willReturn(aResponse()
                .withHeader("X-Cache", "HIT")
                .withBody("{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"John\"}")));
    }
}
```

**Key Insight:** Mocks are code and deserve the same care as production code. Keep them simple, document them, version them, and monitor them. The goal is mocks that are reliable enough to trust, yet flexible enough to evolve as your understanding of the system grows.

Mocha is a feature-rich JavaScript test framework, and Chai is an assertion library. Together with Supertest for HTTP assertions, they form a powerful JavaScript API testing stack.

