                },
                'Integration Tests': {
                    catchError(buildResult: 'UNSTABLE', stageResult: 'FAILURE') {
                        sh 'pytest tests/integration'
                    }
                }
            ]

            parallel parallelStages
        }
    }
    post {
        always {
            script {
                // Check overall result
                if (currentBuild.result == 'UNSTABLE') {
                    echo 'Some tests failed, but pipeline continues'
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

**Key Insight:** Parallel execution transforms hour-long test suites into minute-long feedback cycles. The key is intelligent test splitting—balancing load across workers to minimize total execution time. Start with simple splits by directory, then evolve to data-driven load balancing.

